","value":"+4%","icon":"DMGAmp.webp"},{"name":"DMGAmp","value":"+4%","icon":"DMGAmp.webp"},{"name":"DMGAmp","value":"+4%","icon":"DMGAmp.webp"},{"name":"DMGAmp","value":"+4%","icon":"DMGAmp.webp"}],"b":[{"name":"AllATK%","value":"+12%","icon":"AllATKpct.webp"},{"name":"AllATK%","value":"+12%","icon":"AllATKpct.webp"},{"name":"AllATK%","value":"+12%","icon":"AllATKpct.webp"},{"name":"AllATK%","value":"+12%","icon":"AllATKpct.webp"}],"second":"no","why_by_stat":{"DMGAmp":"Increases all damage dealt by Xiao Qiao by the given %, making it useful for both general damage and higher PVE scores. Also increases DOT damage."},"story":"\"I figured you'll need to keep taking these for a while —at least until you adjust to the powers— so I made a whole batch for you.\"\n\"Aw, Bi Dam...!\"\n\nWhile taking care of Xiao Qiao as she suffered from effects of the Curse of Destruction, Bi Dam presented her with a gift: a batch of golden pills he personally concocted himself. Deeply moved by Bi Dam's seemingly nonchalant yet gentle treatment —not to mention his striking good looks— Xiao Qiao was convinced that Bi Dam held a special place in his heart for her as well. Bi Dam insists he would've extended this gesture of care to anybody, but Xiao Qiao chose to revel in the blissful illusion of her own making."},"used_in":[{"tip":"Raid: Iron Devourer","cat":"pve","banner":"RAID_ID.webp"},{"tip":"Advent Expedition: God of Destruction","cat":"pve","banner":"ADVENT_GOD.webp"},{"tip":"Advent Expedition: Teo","cat":"pve","banner":"ADVENT_TEO.webp"},{"tip":"Castle Rush: Kris","cat":"pve","banner":"CR_KRIS.webp"},{"tip":"Tower of Trials","cat":"pve","banner":"TOWER_OF_TRIALS.webp"},{"tip":"Adventure (Both)","cat":"pve","banner":"ADVENTURE_BOTH.webp"},{"tip":"Power Up Dungeon: Gold","cat":"pve","banner":"PU_DUNGEON_GOLD.webp"}],"lore":"Although still young, Xiao Qiao and her older sister Da Qiao were so renowned for their beauty that they were called the \"beautiful sisters\" in nearby villages.\nBut despite her soft appearance, Xiao Qiao was quite the tomboy.\nShe once stole a monster bird's egg, which caused the monster bird to rampage all the way into the village. And when the village's livestock were attacked by wolves, she spent several days tracking them down to take revenge.\nFortunately, she was skilled enough to defeat the invading monster bird and eventually wiped out the wolf packs.\nHowever, her parents hoped she behave calmly and marry into a good family.\nHer spirited and reckless behavior is a constant source of concern."}